n\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\nSearch\nSearch\nElections Director\nFabienne Dellinger\nDirector\n200 Montezuma Street, Newland NC 28657\n828-733-8282\n828-733-8283\nfabienne.dellinger@averycountync.gov\nHours\nMon-Fri\n8:00AM-4:30PM\nRelated Pages\nStaff\nAvery County Election Results\nCheck Voter Registration (Look Up Sample Ballot)\nNC Voter Registration Application\nAbsentee Ballot Request Form\nNC Elections Facebook Page\nNC Elections Twitter Page\nCandidate Guide\nPhoto ID Overview\nAvery County Voting Precinct Maps\nUOCAVA Election Notice\nBoard of Elections\nHome\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections Office\nPutting Citizens First...\nAvery County nurtures a sense of community by providing services and activities in a cost-effective and efficient manner reflecting proper stewardship of public trust.\nThe Avery County Board of Elections conducts Federal, State and County elections. This department has the responsibility for the administration of voter registration, the electoral process, and campaign finance disclosures. The Elections office registers all eligible voters who meet residency and age requirements, tallies election results, and maintains a record of all registered voters in the County.\nThe Board of Elections operates under a five-member board appointed by the State Board of Elections. Board meetings are held regularly and dates are posted at the courthouse. Specific information pertaining to the registration and electoral process may be seen on subsequent pages within the Board of Elections portion of the County Website.\nBoard Meetings:\nMeetings are held in the Board of Elections office located in the Avery County Government Courthouse Annex Suite 307 at 200 Montezuma St. Newland, NC.\nCurrent board members are:\nCrystal L. Vance\nChairperson\nPaisley King\nMember\nGary McClure\nMember\nMinnie Johnson\nMember\nAlton Medlin\nMember\nNext Meetings of the Board of Elections:\nOctober 13th at 5:00 pm at the Avery County Board of Elections Office ( 200 Montezuma St., Suite 307, Newland, NC 28657)\nOctober 20th at 5:00 pm at the Avery County Board of Elections Office ( 200 Montezuma St., Suite 307, Newland, NC 28657)\nOctober 27th at 5:00 pm at the Avery County Board of Elections Office ( 200 Montezuma St., Suite 307, Newland, NC 28657)\nUpcoming Event(s):\nEarly Voting begins October 15th\nEarly Voting ends October 31st\nElection Day is November 3rd\nNew Voter ID Requirement:\nhttps://www.ncsbe.gov/voting/voter-id\nCandidate Filing Fee is 1% of the annual base salary for all offices sought.\nADDITIONAL DEPARTMENT INFORMATION:\nMailing Address:\nPO Box 145\nNewland, NC 28657\nVoter Registration:\nYou may register to vote in North Carolina at the Board of Elections Office in Newland, NC. You may also register to vote at the Department of Motor Vehicles Office when conducting official DMV business, or at a state agency when applying for benefits.\nVoting Deadlines:\nThe deadline to register to vote in North Carolina and in Avery County is 25 days before the date of an election. Forms must be received in the Elections Office or postmarked by the deadline. Each voter will be sent a voter card showing his/her assigned precinct.\nTo be eligible to vote you must...\nBe a citizen of the United States\nBe a resident of North Carolina and Avery County for at least 30 days prior to an election.\nBe at least 18 years of age by the next general election.\nNot be registered to vote in another county or state.\nIf convicted of a felony, have had your citizenship rights restored.\nIf you move to another county in North Carolina, you will need to register in that county.\nOne-Stop Absentee Voting\nClick\nOne Stop Voting\nfor more information on One Stop Absentee Voting or call our office at 828-733-8282.\nFAQ:\nWhat should I do if I do not have an N.C. driver\u2019s license/DMV ID number or a social security number?\nIf you have neither of these numbers, you may be asked to provide an alternative form of personal identification when you next vote, if you have not done so already. Election officials call this a \u201cHAVA ID,\u201d based on the acronym for the federal law that requires this form of identification \u2014 the Help America Vote Act.\nWhat is a HAVA ID document?\nA HAVA ID document is a document that proves your identity. It can be a current and valid photo ID, or it can be one of the following documents that is current and includes your name and address:\nUtility bill: Telephone, mobile phone, electric, gas, cable television, water, sewage, internet\nBank statement or bank-issued credit card statement\nPaycheck or paycheck stub from an employer or a W-2 statement\nGovernment paycheck, invoice, letter, or any other document from a local, state, or U.S. government agency\nOther government documents: Property tax bill; license to hunt, fish, own a gun; auto registration; public housing or social service agency document\nPlease note that the document must be current.\nWhat is a current HAVA ID document?\nTo be\ncurrent\n, the document must be unexpired, if it has an expiration date. If the document does not have an expiration date, the issuance date must be within six months of the date it is presented to the election official. If a document does not have an issuance date or expiration date, there must be other time-based indicators on the document showing that it is current.\nPRECINCTS:\nThere are 19 precincts in Avery County:\n(01) Altamont\n(02) Banner Elk\n(03) Beech Mountain\n(04) Cary\u2019s Flat\n(05) Cranberry\n(06) Elk Park\n(07) Frank\n(08) Heaton\n(09) Hughes\n(10) Ingalls\n(11) Linville\n(12) Minneapolis\n(13) Montezuma\n(14) Newland 1\n(15) Newland 2\n(16) Pineola\n(17) Plumtree *Plumtree Presbyterian Church\n(18) Pyatte\n(19) Roaring Creek\nMUNICIPALITIES:\nThere are 8 Municipalities in Avery County:\nCrossnore:\nCrossnore Meeting House - 1 Fountain Circle, Crossnore, NC\nBanner Elk, Seven Devils, Beech Mountain:\nBanner Elk Town Hall - 200 Park Avenue, Banner Elk, NC\nElk Park:\nElk Park Town Hall - 169 Winters St, Elk Park, NC\nNewland:\nAvery Morrison Library - 150 Library Place, Newland, NC\nSugar Mtn.:\nSugar Mtn. Town Hall - 251 Dick Trundy Ln, Banner Elk, NC\nGrandfather Village:\nLinville Fire Dept. - 590 NC Hwy 105, Linville, NC\nAvery County Administration\nPh:\n828-733-8201\nView Directory\nFacebook\nYoutube\nResources\nEconomic Development\nDepartments\nHave Questions?\nContact Us\nPowered by\nrevize.,\nGovernment Website Experts\nLogin\nShare this page\nClose\nPlease ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of\nwebsite accessibility",
